<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achaeus (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 213 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Achaeus was a Seleucid general and a cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> who restored Seleucid control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> in the 220s BCE. In 220 BCE he proclaimed himself king, and his forces campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisidia">Pisidia</a>, besieging Selge in 218 BCE. Antiochus besieged him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a>, and after his capture in 213 BCE he was executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achaeus-general.jpg" alt="Achaeus (general)" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.arsclassicacoins.com/ · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tetradrachm_-_Achaios_Usurper.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
